 "synthesis": "# Bullish Structure Ranking — 2026-08-18 EOD (Skylit)\n\n1. **TSM** — Massive 3d squeeze: -10.32G negative gamma at 440 (2%) sits directly under a monster +667.96 vanna magnet at 450 (4.3%), the single largest vanna print in the entire dataset — dealers forced to chase into size.\n\n2. **DRAM** — Near-ATM barney: -56.55G at 60 (-1.1%, essentially spot) plus -15.48G at 62 (2.2%) is the tightest, largest negative-gamma cluster right at price seen anywhere — textbook squeeze ignition zone, with 65 vanna (+55.28, 7.1%) as the follow-through magnet.\n\n3. **MSFT** — 480 pin (+34.14G) anchors spot, but -7.62G squeeze at 490 (2.1%) is backed by a huge -328.2 vanna wall at 500 (4.1%) — mega-cap size means this hedging flow moves real dollars.\n\n4. **NKE** — Sharp squeeze at 40 (1.9%, -9.55G) sits right on top of spot with matching -22.53 vanna — clean, close, high-conviction gamma flip zone for a small-price name.\n\n5. **PLTR** — 180 strike (4.9%) carries both negative gamma (-4.58) and negative vanna (-69.96), a coincident squeeze/magnet combo just above spot — dealers short gamma into a real vanna wall.\n\n6. **PYPL** — 62.5 (3.4%) negative gamma (-9.52) matched by -47.64 vanna is proportionally one of the largest squeeze setups relative to the stock's book — near-dated, sizable, and close to spot.\n\n7. **NVDA** — No clean squeeze, but stacked vanna magnets at 227.5/230/232.5 (1-3.3%) sit right above spot with a giant +49G pin at 227.5 — dealer-supported melt-up path is short and well-defined.\n\n8. **DIS** — 105 (1.3%) shows tight negative gamma (-2.96) directly over spot with matching -17.27 vanna, plus a bigger 110 (6.1%) vanna magnet (+63.23) as secondary target.\n\n9. **BMNR** — 19 strike (1.2%) negative gamma (-4.65) essentially at spot, feeding into 20 (+5.55 vanna, 6.5%) — small-cap but very near-dated squeeze geometry.\n\n10. **VST** — 155 (5.7%) negative gamma (-2.21) aligned with -37.19 vanna gives a coherent, if slightly farther, squeeze/magnet combo above spot.\n\nTOP10: TSM,DRAM,MSFT,NKE,PLTR,PYPL,NVDA,DIS,BMNR,VST"
